Pointer routing must survive the HID++ capture session's lifecycle.

Ordinary pointer input arrives through the OS hook; the HID++ session only adds
diverted controls (gesture button, thumbwheel, DPI buttons) and is re-armed
whenever the device idles. The bridge used to require that session for a
capture lease and to fault the lease when the session restarted, which kicked
hidpipe back to local mode every re-arm.

